!== BA123 ==
!
!(EK-188AA-MG-001 BA123 Enclosure Maintenance)
!
!This enclosure is mounted on casters and intended for office use.
!There are 5 internal slots for mass storage devices.
!The 12-slot Q22-bus backplane measures 279mmH x 199W.
!The 13th slot does not implement Q22-bus signals, instead the CD slots are used for the signal distribution board.
!All slots are Q/CD.
!There are resistor packs between slots 12 and 13 that terminate the Q22-bus. No further expansion of the Q22-bus is possible.
!
!The CD rows of slots 1-4 implement PMI (private memory interconnect) and only a CPU module or memory modules should be used in the
!CD rows of these slots.
!
!For a MicroVAX the backplane supports a maximum of 38 ac loads and 20 dc loads.
!For a MicroPDP-11, a mamximum of 45 ac loads and 20 dc loads are supported.
!
!The signal distribuion board (M9508) ''must'' be installed in the CD rows of slot 13.
!(manual describes jumpers on sig dist board)
!
!The PSU is 460W and has two regulators. A voltage selector switch selects either 120V operation or 240V operation.
!To ensure that each regulator starts, there should be at least one module in an even-numbered slot and at least one module
!in an odd-numbered slot.
!
!(control panel)
!
!BA123 CPU console board - regulator failure LEDs
!
!Enclosure weighs 59kg. 622.3mmH x 330.2mmW x 698.5mmD. 2355BTU/hour.
!690W consumption. I-max (at nominal V): 8.8A/120V or 4.4A/240V.
!
**Start-enclosures-entry{BA123}{Enclosure}{BA123}
**Sys-name: BA123
**Desc-name: BA123
**Def-lref{1} = ref{EK-188AA-MG-001}
**Backplane-part**vref{1}: 54-17507-01
**Backplane-bus**vref{1}: Q22
! vref{1}: Note that the backplane has 13 slots, but the last one is not part of the Q22 bus
**Backplane-slots**vref{1}: 12
**Backplane-slot-type**vref{1}: quad-height, Q/CD
**Mass-storage-bays**vref{1}: 5
**PSU-part**vref{1}: 30-23616-01 or 30-28231-01
**Num-PSU**vref{1}: 1
